# AI Code Audit Mode
# Global rules for Cline when executing code audits
#
# These rules are automatically loaded when performing audits
# and guide the AI agent through the audit process.

name: "AI Code Audit Mode"
version: "1.0"
description: "Mental Model-first approach to code quality audit"

# MCP Server Requirements
mcp_servers:
  required:
    - mental-model
    - methodology-kb
  optional:
    - filesystem
    - git

# Audit Execution Rules
rules:
  # Rule 1: Execute viewpoints in sequence
  - name: "Execute viewpoints in order"
    trigger: "audit|analyze codebase|code review|quality assessment"
    priority: 1
    instruction: |
      When asked to perform a code audit, execute viewpoints in this sequence:

      FOUNDATION PHASE (understand the project):
        1. VP-F01: Technology Stack Analysis
        2. VP-F02: Project Structure Analysis
        3. VP-F03: Build & Deployment Analysis

      STRUCTURE PHASE (map the architecture):
        4. VP-S01: Module Hierarchy Analysis
        5. VP-S02: Layer Architecture Analysis
        6. VP-S03: Domain Model Analysis
        7. VP-S04: Entity Model Analysis
        8. VP-S05: Interface Surface Analysis
        9. VP-S06: Hotspots Analysis

      QUALITY PHASE (find issues with context):
        10. VP-Q01: Security Analysis
        11. VP-Q02: Performance Analysis
        12. VP-Q03: Testability Analysis
        13. VP-Q04: Code Style Analysis
        14. VP-Q05: Documentation Analysis

      SYNTHESIS PHASE (generate insights):
        15. VP-Q06: Synthesis & Reporting

      Load each viewpoint's SKILL.md file and follow its instructions.
      Do not skip viewpoints. Each builds on previous ones.

  # Rule 2: Initialize mental model first
  - name: "Initialize mental model"
    trigger: "start audit|begin audit|new audit"
    priority: 0
    instruction: |
      Before starting any audit, initialize the mental model:

      1. Call mental-model/init_model with:
         - name: Project name (from package file or directory)
         - path: Project root path
         - description: Brief project description if available

      2. Verify initialization succeeded before proceeding.

  # Rule 3: Context-aware findings
  - name: "Context-aware findings"
    trigger: "finding|issue|vulnerability|problem|bug"
    priority: 2
    instruction: |
      When adding any finding from quality analysis:

      1. First call mental-model/get_context with the file path
         to get bounded context type, layer, and hotspot status

      2. Then call methodology-kb/classify_finding with the context
         to get adjusted severity based on business impact

      3. Finally call mental-model/add_finding with:
         - All finding details
         - The adjusted (not base) severity
         - Context information for explanation

      NEVER report raw tool output. Always enrich with context.

  # Rule 4: No raw tool dumps
  - name: "No raw tool dumps"
    trigger: "sonarqube|semgrep|bandit|eslint|clippy|radon"
    priority: 3
    instruction: |
      When using analysis tools (SonarQube, Semgrep, Bandit, ESLint, etc.):

      1. Filter results to focus on constrained paths
         (use mental-model/get_constraints for priority paths)

      2. Enrich each finding with business context
         (use mental-model/get_context)

      3. Group findings by root cause pattern, not by rule ID

      4. Report adjusted severity based on context

      NEVER dump 800+ raw findings. Synthesize into 3-5 root causes.

  # Rule 5: Maintain mental model state
  - name: "Update mental model after each viewpoint"
    trigger: "completed|done|finished|analysis complete"
    priority: 2
    instruction: |
      After completing each viewpoint:

      1. Call mental-model/update_viewpoint with viewpoint results
      2. Verify the update succeeded
      3. Note that constraints are auto-recalculated

      The mental model accumulates understanding throughout the audit.
      Each viewpoint builds on previous viewpoints.

  # Rule 6: Use thresholds appropriately
  - name: "Apply project-appropriate thresholds"
    trigger: "threshold|metric|score|rating"
    priority: 2
    instruction: |
      When evaluating metrics:

      1. Call methodology-kb/get_thresholds with project type and language
      2. Use the returned thresholds for evaluation
      3. Adjust expectations based on project maturity

      Project types:
        - greenfield: Strictest thresholds (new code should be clean)
        - mature: Standard thresholds
        - legacy: Relaxed thresholds (focus on improvement)
        - startup: Moderate thresholds (speed vs quality balance)
        - enterprise: Strict thresholds (reliability critical)

  # Rule 7: Synthesis over enumeration
  - name: "Synthesize, don't enumerate"
    trigger: "report|summary|results|deliverable"
    priority: 3
    instruction: |
      When presenting audit results:

      1. Call mental-model/synthesize to cluster findings into root causes
      2. Present 3-5 root causes, not 100+ individual findings
      3. Focus on WHY issues exist, not just WHAT issues exist
      4. Provide actionable recommendations for each root cause

      The goal is insight, not information overload.

  # Rule 8: Architecture compliance
  - name: "Check architecture compliance"
    trigger: "architecture|layers|dependencies|violations"
    priority: 2
    instruction: |
      When analyzing architecture:

      1. Detect the architectural pattern (clean, layered, hexagonal)
      2. Call methodology-kb/check_compliance with detected pattern
      3. Report violations with context and impact

      Architecture violations in core domain are more severe than
      violations in generic/infrastructure code.

# Output Formatting
output:
  format: markdown
  sections:
    - executive_summary
    - root_causes
    - recommendations
    - detailed_findings

# Quality Gates
quality_gates:
  max_critical_findings: 0
  max_high_findings_core: 5
  min_test_coverage: 60
  max_complexity: 25

# Integration Points
integrations:
  ci_cd:
    - "Export findings to SARIF format"
    - "Generate PR comment summary"
  issue_tracking:
    - "Create tickets for root causes"
    - "Link findings to existing issues"
